+
+		/* The RESET line is ACTIVE LOW but the kernel driver has inverted logic.
+		 * The driver for the I2C eusb2 repeater calls:
+		 * gpiod_set_value_cansleep(er->reset_gpiod, bring_out_of_reset=true);
+		 * Technically this is ASSERTING the reset line. (ie holding the device in reset...)
+		 * When it really should be DE-ASSERTING (ie taking the device out of reset).
+		 * So we must set the reset GPIO to be ACTIVE HIGH in the device tree
+		 * so that the driver set's this pin HIGH to bring out of reset.
